@@@!atrep

@@/ at-drama: the drama pack - acts, scenes, prose and verse
@@/ dialogue, dramatis personae, stage directions and their
@@/ inline kin.
@@/ Part of the standard library; composes with koine and its
@@/ sibling packs.

@=== act
@:=[(taxis)] [lemma]
grammata
=:@
@"drama act"@
===@

@=== scene
@:#[(taxis)] [lemma]
grammata
#:@
@"drama scene"@
===@

@=== dialogue
@: lemma
grammata
:@
@"drama dialogue; the lemma is the speech prefix"@
===@

@=== verse-dialogue
@:~ lemma
stichos
~:@
@"drama dialogue in verse (PROVISIONAL: F1, F2)"@
===@

@=== dramatis-persona
@:! grammata !:@
@"dramatis personae entry, bare (name only), own paragraph"@
===@

@=== character
@:!! lemma
grammata
!!:@
@"dramatis personae entry with description (TENTATIVE symbol)"@
@""
The lemma is the character name; the grammata is the
description, possibly multi-paragraph.
""@
===@

@=== stage-direction
@:( grammata ):@
@"inline stage direction; also the action beat in prose"@
===@

@=== stage-direction-block
@:[
grammata
]:@
@"block stage direction"@
===@

@=== dialogue-line
@:- grammata -:@
@"prose-fiction dialogue line, own paragraph"@
@""
Semantic marker only; quotation marks or leading em-dashes are
entered by the author per the language's convention.
""@
===@

@=== dialogue-tag
@:_ grammata _:@
@"dialogue tag (attribution) within a dialogue line"@
@""
Includes trailing punctuation, excludes leading punctuation.
""@
@^(:-)
===@

@=== pause
@:. grammata .:@
@"dramatic pause (TENTATIVE symbol)"@
@""
Stands alone as a paragraph in drama and prose; canonical
grammata is a literal ellipsis. Local, unlike the structural
section-break. Genoses may refine typesetting.
""@
===@
